    2. Pick num_marked from {4,5}; mark odd rows 1,3,5,7 (and 9 if 5).
    3. Pick num_match from 0..num_marked (prefer 0-2 for variety).
    4. Choose num_match rows to be matching; rest are mismatching.
    5. Sample 4-5 distinct non-zero colors. For each marked row, assign left/right from the color pool -- matching rows get same color both sides, mismatching rows get two different colors.
    6. Place markers at (row, 0) and (row, W-1).
